**/.pbi/localSettings.json
**/.pbi/cache.abf

# Ephemeral agent worktrees (Claude Code agent isolation)
.claude/worktrees/

# Deployment generated artifacts (snapshots and reports)
products/fabric/powerbi/deployment/snapshots/
products/fabric/powerbi/deployment/reports/

# Theme-Engine-Ausgabe auf Abruf (apply_report_theme --run-generator, derive_brand_artifacts):
# ALUCA-eigen, reproduzierbar, nicht versioniert. Vendorte Themes: products/fabric/powerbi/themes/
products/fabric/powerbi/themes_local/

# Generated review outputs
internal/reviews/*.md
!internal/reviews/full_repo_quality_audit.md

# Node.js dependencies (reproducible via npm ci)
tooling/validation/node_modules/

# Generated validation results (produced by Stage 1 runner)
tooling/validation/results/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Python virtual environments (bootstrap)
tooling/.venv/
.venv/

# Stray pip install metadata (should never be committed into the tree)
*.dist-info/

# Generated registry outputs (produced by registry_builder.py)
tooling/ontology/out/

# Generated IR outputs (derived from registry outputs)
tooling/ir/out/

# Customer export packages (generated)
dist/customer_exports/
# Visual Library standalone skill bundle (generated by package_skill.py)
tooling/visual_library/dist/

# Local env (token etc.) – never commit
.env
.env.local

# Project snapshot for Assistant briefing (generated by refresh_project_snapshot.ps1)
internal/project_mgmt/PROJECT_SNAPSHOT.md

# Local-only tool outputs: Desktop error log, validation/publish results, publish
# staging, TMDL renderer log (see products/fabric/powerbi/docs/references/powerbi-modeling-mcp-setup.md)
.local/
# Cursor is no longer used here; keep a stray local .cursor/ out of the repo
.cursor/

# Root-level registry outputs (ignore if someone runs registry_builder without --out-dir)
master_registry.json
value_map.json
governance_gaps.json
orphans_report.json
# Root-level Node artifacts (Studio lives in /studio)
node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json

# Next.js build artifacts
studio/.next/

# Studio local/dev artifacts (should not be committed)
# - SQLite WAL/SHM files created by better-sqlite3
studio/data/*.db-wal
studio/data/*.db-shm
studio/data/*.db-journal

# - Playwright local report/test run metadata
# Playwright-Artefakte: der ganze Baum, nicht nur zwei Dateien. Beide waren zusaetzlich
# *getrackt* — dann greift .gitignore nicht, und jeder lokale e2e-Lauf machte den Baum
# schmutzig (gemessen 01.08.2026). Untracked + Verzeichnis-Ignore statt Datei-Ignore.
studio/playwright-report/
studio/test-results/

# CI run logs (local only – not versioned)
internal/metrics/runs/*.json
internal/metrics/runs/**/*.json
internal/metrics/generation_runs/*.json

# Desktop Bridge screenshots (R4.1) — local proof-of-work, not versioned;
# attach/paste into the PR or ledger entry instead of committing PNGs.
internal/metrics/desktop_screenshots/

# Backup files
*.bak

# External tool binaries (download via .tools/README.md; not committed)
.tools/pbi-tools/
.tools/fab-inspector/
.tools/dotnet/
.tools/*.zip
drift_report.json

# Local agent / IDE artifacts (machine-specific, never commit)
.claude/settings.local.json
.pytest_cache/

# Python build artifacts (`python -m build`) — root-anchored so the tracked
# products/fabric/powerbi/dist/ is never affected
/build/
/*.egg-info/
/dist/*.whl
/dist/*.tar.gz


# START Ruler Generated Files
/.agent/rules/ruler.md
/.amazonq/mcp.json
/.amazonq/rules/ruler_q_rules.md
/.augment/rules/ruler_augment_instructions.md
/.clinerules
/.crush.json
/.goosehints
/.idx/airules.md
/.junie/guidelines.md
/.kiro/steering/ruler_kiro_instructions.md
/.openhands/microagents/repo.md
/.trae/rules/project_rules.md
/CRUSH.md
/WARP.md
/firebender.json
# END Ruler Generated Files

KPI_Framework_Discovery_*.xlsx

# Real, customer-specific showcases stay LOCAL — per showcases/README.md §Scope
# ("Customer-specific implementations … kept in separate project repositories").
# Only the synthetic demo (aurora_group) + the archived structural sample are tracked.
/showcases/*/
!/showcases/aurora_group/
!/showcases/sample_pbip_report/

# Kundenkennungen, niemals versionieren (04.09.2026). Die Liste ist die einzige
# Stelle, an der echte Namen stehen duerfen; Vorlage unter scripts/.
.kundendaten-sperrliste.json

# Agenten-Ablagen und Testlaeufe (07.09.2026). Nichts davon ist Quelle: `.codex/` und
# `Claude outputs/` sind Kratzflaechen laufender Agenten, `studio/.e2e/` ist der
# Ausgabeordner von Playwright (7,4 MB Bilder je Lauf). Sie standen als untracked im
# Status und waeren beim naechsten `git add -A` mitgekommen.
.codex/
Claude outputs/
studio/.e2e/

# Arbeitsordner der agentischen Schleife (AP-9): Manifest, PBIP-Kopien, Seitenbilder, befunde.json.
# Ins Repo kommt davon nur, was bewusst uebernommen wird (Plan §5), nie der ganze Lauf.
/out/agentic_loop/
